# End User License Agreement — Logiqum Software

**Draft v1.0 · 2026-10-16 · Effective 2026-10-16 · Governing entity: Logiqum Kft. (Logiqum Korlátolt Felelősségű Társaság), 2094 Nagykovácsi, Berkenye utca 8., Hungary · Company reg. no. 13-09-246330 · Tax no. 33020983-2-13**

This End User License Agreement ("**Agreement**") is a binding contract between **Logiqum Kft.**
("**Logiqum**", "we", "us") and the individual or entity that installs, downloads, accesses, or uses
the Software ("**Customer**", "you"). **By installing, downloading, activating, or using the Software,
you agree to this Agreement.** If you are accepting on behalf of an organization, you represent that you
have authority to bind it. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software. This Agreement is
for business use; the Software is not intended for consumers.

---

## 1. Definitions

- **Software** — the Logiqum log-intelligence platform ("**logrok**") and the Logiqum universal agent
  ("**LUnA** / logrok-universal-agent"), the **Converter** and the **Tools** (both defined below), in
  object-code form, plus Documentation and any updates we provide. The Software is **proprietary and closed-source**; it is licensed, not sold.
- **Agent** — the LUnA endpoint software component.
- **Converter** — `luna-migrate`, the separate configuration-converter tool that Logiqum publishes with
  each LUnA release, together with its Go packages and mapping logic, and any successor or similar
  converter we ship.
- **Tools** — the Logiqum command-line and helper programs that ship with the Software, such as
  `logrokctl` and the other administration, diagnostic, import, and validation utilities in the
  distribution, whether or not the Documentation lists each one.
- **Converted Configuration** — the configuration files and reports a Converter or Tool produces from
  Customer's own input configuration. Converted Configuration is Customer Data: Customer owns it and
  may use, modify, and keep it after this Agreement ends. The Converter, the Tools, and their mapping
  logic, rules, and tables are Software and Logiqum Content, and are not Customer Data even though
  Converted Configuration is produced by them.
- **Documentation** — the then-current published usage documentation for the Software.
- **Order** — an order form, quote, or online purchase referencing this Agreement that specifies the
  purchased tier, term, quantities (e.g. agents / Log Source Hosts), and Fees.
- **Entitlement** — the cryptographically-signed license record that authorizes a tier and/or
  capabilities, verified by the Software **offline** (see §4).
- **Free Tier ("Core")** — the no-charge capability level defined in the Documentation.
- **Paid Tier ("Apex")** — the paid capability level, unlocked by a valid Entitlement per an Order.
- **Evaluation** — a time-limited, no-charge grant of Paid-Tier capabilities for assessment.
- **Customer Data** — log data, events, and other content that Customer or its systems feed into or
  store with the Software, and results the Software derives from it for Customer.
- **Affiliate** — an entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with a party,
  where control means owning more than 50% of the voting interests.
- **Authorized Users** — Customer's and its Affiliates' employees and individual contractors whom
  Customer permits to use the Software on Customer's behalf.
- **Open-Source Component** — any software, library, rule set, or data file included with or used by
  the Software that is made available under an open-source or other public license (for example, the
  GNU GPL or LGPL, Apache 2.0, MIT, BSD, MPL, AGPL, or the Detection Rule License), as listed in the
  third-party notices and open-source inventory published in the Documentation.
- **Logiqum Interfaces** — the non-public communication protocols, message and wire formats, APIs,
  file and storage formats, and license-file formats used by or between components of the Software
  (for example, Agent enrollment, configuration, heartbeat, and relay exchanges with the control
  plane, on-disk spool and buffer formats, and the Entitlement format), excluding open standards the
  Software implements (such as RFC 5424 syslog, OTLP, or HTTP) and interfaces the Documentation
  publishes for customer integration.
- **Logiqum Content** — the detection rules, correlation logic, parsers, models, dashboards, reports,
  templates, and other content that Logiqum authors and ships with or for the Software, excluding
  Open-Source Components.
- **Operational Data** — non-content telemetry about the Software's own operation (see §5); expressly
  **not** Customer's log data or other Customer Data.

## 2. License grant (tiered)

Subject to this Agreement, Logiqum grants Customer a **revocable, limited, non-exclusive,
non-transferable, non-sublicensable** license to install and use the Software, as follows:

- **(a) Free Tier ("Core")** — you may use the Free-Tier capabilities of the Software at no charge if
  **any** of the following applies: (i) your use is **non-commercial**; (ii) the Agent is used together
  with a validly-licensed logrok deployment ("**bundled with logrok**"); or (iii) your commercial,
  standalone use does not exceed **ten (10)** Agents. This is a perpetual grant for so long as you
  comply with this Agreement.
- **(b) Paid Tier ("Apex")** — you may use the Paid-Tier capabilities during the term of, and to the
  quantities stated in, an Order for which Fees are paid, unlocked by your Entitlement.
- **(c) Evaluation** — if we provide an Evaluation, you may use the stated capabilities for the
  evaluation period, solely for **internal evaluation** in a non-production capacity. Evaluations are
  provided **AS IS** with no warranty, support, indemnity, or SLA (§8, §9, §10 notwithstanding, the
  liability cap for Evaluation is **US$500**).
- **(d) Bundled with logrok** — where the Agent is bundled with a logrok subscription, the Agent
  capabilities licensed by that subscription carry **no separate Agent fee**; the applicable logrok
  Order governs quantities (e.g. Log Source Hosts).

Use exceeding your Entitlement or the conditions above requires a corresponding Order.

**(e) Internal business purposes.** Every grant in this §2 is for Customer's **internal business
purposes** only — processing Customer's own data, and data Customer is lawfully entitled to process, for
Customer's own operations — unless an Order expressly authorizes use on behalf of third parties (for
example, a managed-security-service Order). A license granted for one purpose (for example, a Free-Tier,
Evaluation, development, or non-production instance) may not be used for another (for example,
production, marketing, demonstration to third parties, or competitive work).

**(f) Authorized Users and Affiliates.** Customer may let Authorized Users, including contractors
operating the Software for Customer, use the Software on Customer's behalf. Customer is responsible for
their compliance and is liable for their acts and omissions as for its own.

## 3. Capability enforcement by license key

Capabilities above the Free Tier are gated by the Entitlement / license-key functionality in the
Software. You may **not** move, change, disable, remove, obscure, or otherwise circumvent that
functionality, nor use or access any capability you are not licensed for. Circumventing the license-key
functionality is a **material breach** of this Agreement.

Without limiting the above, you will not: (a) create, alter, forge, or share license files or
Entitlements, or use an Entitlement issued for another person or deployment; (b) tamper with clocks,
trial or grace-period state, installation fingerprints, or counters the Software uses to apply its
Entitlement; (c) start a further Evaluation for the same deployment by reinstalling, wiping, cloning, or
otherwise resetting it; (d) exceed, or disguise use above, the licensed quantities (for example, by
aggregating many sources behind one counted source to avoid counting them); or (e) distribute or use any
tool, patch, or instruction whose purpose is to do any of the above. That the Software cannot
technically prevent an action does not make the action permitted.

## 4. Offline licensing — no phone-home *(differentiator; keep)*

The Software is **air-gapped-ready by design**. The Entitlement is verified **entirely offline** by
cryptographic signature; the Software **does not require, and the license grant is not conditioned on,
any connection to Logiqum or any external license server**. For air-gapped or disconnected deployments,
Logiqum provides an **offline license file** that the operator installs; the Software verifies it locally
and, on validity, unlocks the licensed tier. Expiry or invalidity of an Entitlement causes the Software
to **fall back to the Free Tier**, not to cease functioning. No feature of this Agreement obligates the
Software to "call home" to remain licensed.

## 5. Telemetry — opt-in, and never license-gating *(drafted fresh; keep)*

The Software **does not transmit Operational Data to Logiqum by default.** Optional product telemetry
may be **enabled by the operator** ("opt-in"); when enabled, it transmits only **Operational Data**
(e.g. Software version, enabled-feature flags, error and throughput counts) and **never Customer log
content or personal data of data subjects**. Operator may disable it at any time, and it is disabled in
air-gapped deployments. **Disabling or the unavailability of telemetry does not disable, degrade, throttle,
or otherwise affect the Software or the license.** Managed-agent enrollment, heartbeat, and metrics are
exchanged only with **Customer's own** logrok control plane and remain within Customer's environment;
they are not transmitted to Logiqum. Operational Data that Customer opts to share is not Customer Data.

## 6. Restrictions

### 6.1 Use restrictions

Except as this Agreement or an Order expressly permits, and subject always to §6.2 and §6.3, you will
not, and will not permit or help anyone else to:

- **(a) Copy or modify.** Copy the Software (other than reasonable copies for licensed installation,
  backup, disaster recovery, and non-production testing within your Entitlement), or modify, translate,
  adapt, or create derivative works of it.
- **(b) Distribute or host for others.** Rent, lease, lend, sell, resell, sublicense, assign, distribute,
  publish, or otherwise make the Software available to any third party, or use it to provide a service
  bureau, time-sharing, hosted, or managed service to third parties.
- **(c) Reverse engineer.** Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, decrypt, or otherwise attempt to
  derive the source code, underlying structure, algorithms, or non-public design of the Software,
  **including by analyzing, capturing, replaying, or emulating Logiqum Interfaces** (for example,
  inspecting Agent-to-control-plane traffic or license files in order to reimplement either side), or by
  analyzing its file, storage, spool, or license-file formats.
- **(d) Circumvent.** Circumvent the license-key functionality or Entitlement limits (§3), or any
  technical measure that protects the Software or its integrity (such as code signing or configuration
  signatures).
- **(e) Notices.** Remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, trademark, license, or other proprietary
  notice in or on the Software or Documentation.
- **(f) Compete.** Access or use the Software, Documentation, or Logiqum Content to build, train,
  improve, or operate a competing product or service, to perform competitive analysis, or to copy its
  ideas, features, functions, interfaces, or user-interface design.
- **(g) Publish benchmarks.** Disclose to any third party the results of any benchmark, performance,
  capacity, or comparative test of the Software without Logiqum's prior written consent. You may run such
  tests for your own internal evaluation and share the results within your organization and with your
  professional advisers under confidentiality.
- **(h) Extract content or train models.** Extract, scrape, or bulk-export Logiqum Content, the
  Documentation, or the Software's code or interfaces in order to reproduce them outside the Software,
  or use any of them (or output generated by the Software that reproduces them) as training,
  fine-tuning, evaluation, or retrieval data for any machine-learning or artificial-intelligence model,
  other than a model used by the Software itself as provided. This does not restrict your use of
  Customer Data or of analytic results about Customer Data.
- **(i) Unlawful use.** Use the Software in violation of applicable law, including data-protection,
  privacy, interception, and employee-monitoring laws, or to collect data from systems or persons you are
  not authorized to monitor.
- **(j) Exceed scope.** Use the Software beyond the tier, quantities, term, purposes, or deployment
  your Entitlement and Order allow.
- **(k) AI-assisted replication.** Use any large language model, AI coding assistant, autonomous or
  semi-autonomous AI agent, or other automated system to observe, map, describe, specify, or reproduce
  the Software, its features, functions, workflows, user interface, Logiqum Interfaces, Logiqum Content,
  or Documentation, in order to create, or help create, a product, service, or component that is
  substantially similar to or competes with the Software or any part of it. This includes: (i) feeding
  the Software's code, binaries, configuration it generates, output, screens, traffic, or Documentation
  into such a system as input, context, or a specification for that purpose; (ii) directing such a
  system to operate or probe the Software (through its user interface, APIs, or Logiqum Interfaces) to
  systematically catalogue its behavior for that purpose; and (iii) any "clean-room" or
  specification-first process in which such a system, or a person relying on its output, had that
  access. A process does not become permitted because a person, rather than the AI system, writes the
  final code, or because the result is described as an independent implementation. This does not
  restrict using AI tools to operate, configure, or troubleshoot the Software for your licensed
  purposes, to build integrations through interfaces the Documentation publishes, or to analyze
  Customer Data.

Each of the restrictions above is separate and independent. §6.1(f), §6.1(g), and §6.1(k) survive
termination.

### 6.2 Rights that applicable law guarantees (interoperability)

Nothing in this Agreement restricts any act that applicable law permits notwithstanding a contractual
prohibition, and §6.1 is to be read as applying only to the extent the law allows. In particular, where
Directive 2009/24/EC on the legal protection of computer programs, or a national law implementing it,
applies: (a) a person entitled to use the Software may observe, study, or test its functioning while
performing acts they are entitled to perform, in order to determine the ideas and principles underlying
any element of it; and (b) a licensee, or a person authorized to act on its behalf, may reproduce and
translate the code where indispensable to obtain the information necessary to achieve interoperability
of an independently created program with the Software, provided that the information is not already
readily available to them, the acts are confined to the parts of the Software necessary for
interoperability, and the information obtained is used only for that purpose and is not given to others
or used to develop a substantially similar program, except as that law allows.

**Ask us first.** Logiqum publishes the interfaces intended for customer integration in the
Documentation and will, on written request to contact@logiqum.com, provide reasonably available
interoperability information you are entitled to under applicable law, on reasonable confidentiality
terms. Providing it on request does not condition any statutory right you have.

### 6.3 Open-Source Components

Open-Source Components are licensed to you under their own licenses, not under this Agreement. **Nothing
in this Agreement limits, and none of its restrictions (including §6.1(a), (c), and (h)) applies to, any
right you have under the license of an Open-Source Component**, and where this Agreement conflicts with
such a license as to that component, the open-source license governs that component. In particular:

- Where an Open-Source Component's license entitles you to its corresponding source code (for example,
  the GNU GPL or LGPL), Logiqum's written offer of that source, as stated in the Documentation, applies
  and is not affected by this Agreement.
- Where the Software uses a library under the GNU LGPL, you may modify that library for your own use and
  reverse engineer the Software to the extent necessary to debug such modifications, as that license
  requires.
- Logiqum provides Open-Source Components "AS IS" as part of the Software; §8 and §10 apply to them to
  the extent the applicable open-source license permits.

The Software as a whole, and every part of it that is not an Open-Source Component, remains subject to
this Agreement.

### 6.4 Security testing and vulnerability reports

You may perform security testing (including vulnerability scanning and penetration testing) of your own
deployment of the Software. You will report suspected vulnerabilities in the Software to Logiqum as
described in the security policy in the Documentation and allow a reasonable coordinated-disclosure
period before disclosing them publicly. Security testing does not authorize any act otherwise
restricted by §6.1(b), (d), or (f).

## 7. Ownership

The Software is licensed, not sold. Logiqum and its licensors retain all right, title, and interest in
and to the Software, Documentation, and all intellectual property therein. Customer retains all right,
title, and interest in Customer Data. Logiqum reserves all rights not expressly granted in this
Agreement; no right is granted by implication or estoppel. The Software, its structure and
organization, the Logiqum Interfaces, and Logiqum Content are Logiqum's trade secrets and copyrighted
works.

**Feedback.** You are never required to give Logiqum suggestions, ideas, bug reports, or other feedback
about the Software ("**Feedback**"). If you do, you grant Logiqum a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide,
royalty-free, transferable, and sublicensable license to use, disclose, and exploit the Feedback for any
purpose, without obligation or attribution to you. Feedback is not your Confidential Information, but
Logiqum will not identify you as its source without your consent. Feedback does not include Customer
Data.

**Operational Data.** Where Customer opts in to telemetry (§5), Logiqum may use Operational Data to
operate, support, secure, and improve the Software and may publish it only in aggregated form that
identifies neither Customer nor any individual.

## 8. Warranty & disclaimer

For **paid** Software, Logiqum warrants that, for **ninety (90) days** after initial delivery, the
Software will operate in material conformance with the Documentation; your sole remedy for breach is that
Logiqum will use commercially reasonable efforts to correct the non-conformance or, failing that, refund
the Fees for the non-conforming Software. **Except for the foregoing, the Software is provided "AS IS"
and "AS AVAILABLE", and Logiqum disclaims all other warranties, express, implied, or statutory, including
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and non-infringement, and does not warrant that
operation will be uninterrupted or error-free.** Free-Tier and Evaluation use is provided "AS IS" with no
warranty. The Software is not designed for use where failure could cause death, personal injury, or
severe physical or environmental damage.

## 9. Indemnification

**(a) By Logiqum.** Logiqum will defend Customer against a third-party claim that a **paid** version of
the Software, used per this Agreement and the Documentation and unmodified, infringes that third party's
patent, copyright, or trademark, and will pay damages finally awarded or agreed in settlement. This
indemnity is available to **all paying customers** (no minimum-spend threshold). If the Software is or may
be enjoined, Logiqum may procure the right to continue use, modify or replace it, or terminate and refund
the unused prepaid Fees. Exclusions: claims arising from Customer modifications, combination with non-
Logiqum products, use outside the Documentation, or Customer Data. This §9(a) states Logiqum's entire
liability and Customer's exclusive remedy for infringement. **(b) By Customer.** Customer will defend
Logiqum against third-party claims arising from Customer Data or Customer's use in violation of law or
this Agreement. Each indemnity is conditioned on prompt notice, sole control of defense (with the other
party's reasonable cooperation), and no settlement admitting the indemnified party's liability without
consent.

## 10. Limitation of liability

**To the maximum extent permitted by law: (a) neither party is liable for any indirect, incidental,
special, consequential, punitive, or exemplary damages, or for lost profits, revenue, or data; and (b)
each party's total aggregate liability under this Agreement will not exceed the Fees paid by Customer for
the Software giving rise to the liability in the twelve (12) months preceding the event** (for Free-Tier
use where no Fees are paid, **US$1,000**; for Evaluation, **US$500**). **Excluded from the cap and
the waiver in (a):** amounts owed under an Order; the parties' indemnity obligations (§9); a party's
breach of the other's intellectual-property rights or of confidentiality; and fraud, gross negligence, or
willful misconduct. Nothing limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable (including EU
consumer/mandatory) law.

## 11. Confidentiality

Each party will protect the other's non-public information disclosed under this Agreement with reasonable
care and use it only to perform this Agreement, excluding information that is public, independently
developed, or rightfully received without duty of confidence. Logiqum's Confidential Information
includes the Software's non-public code, internals, and design; the Logiqum Interfaces; license files
and Entitlements; non-public Documentation; the results of any benchmark or test of the Software
(§6.1(g)); and Logiqum's pricing, Order terms, and roadmap. The receiving party will limit access to
those of its personnel, Affiliates, and advisers who need it for this Agreement and are bound by
confidentiality obligations at least as protective, and is responsible for their compliance. A party
may disclose Confidential Information when required by law, regulation, or court order, after giving
the other party prompt notice where lawful and reasonable help to seek protective treatment. These
obligations last for the term of this Agreement and **five (5) years** after it ends, and for trade
secrets for as long as they remain trade secrets. On termination, or on request, the receiving party
will return or destroy the other's Confidential Information, except copies retained in routine backups
or as required by law, which remain protected. Customer Data is Customer's Confidential Information.

## 12. Term, termination & data

This Agreement applies while you use the Software or during any Order term. Either party may terminate for
the other's material breach not cured within **30 days** of notice. On termination you must stop using and
delete the paid Software. Where Logiqum holds any Customer Data (e.g. in a support context), Customer has
**30 days** after termination to retrieve it, after which Logiqum may delete it in the ordinary course.
Termination does not relieve accrued payment obligations.

**Breach of license restrictions.** If Customer breaches §3 or §6.1 (other than an inadvertent quantity
overage that Customer corrects under §13), Logiqum may, on written notice, terminate this Agreement and
every license under it, **including the Free-Tier grant**, if the breach is not cured within **30 days**
of the notice (or immediately, where the breach cannot be cured). Use of the Software in breach of
§3 or §6.1 is outside the scope of the license.

**Suspension of services.** The Software keeps running under its offline Entitlement (§4) and Logiqum
does not disable it remotely. While a material breach (including non-payment) remains uncured after
notice, Logiqum may suspend support, updates, upgrade bundles, and the issuance or renewal of
Entitlements, without liability and without reducing Fees due.

**On termination**, Customer will stop using the affected Software, delete or destroy all copies in its
possession or control (except Open-Source Components, which Customer keeps under their own licenses),
and, on Logiqum's request, certify in writing that it has done so.

§§3, 6.1(f)–(h), 6.3, 7, 8 (disclaimer), 9–11, 13–14, 17, and 18 survive termination.

## 13. Verification (audit)

No more than **once in any 12-month period** and on **at least 15 days'** written notice, Logiqum may
verify Customer's compliance with the licensed quantities and tier, including by requesting a signed
compliance certification. If verification reveals use exceeding the Entitlement, Customer will promptly
order and pay for the excess at Logiqum's then-current list prices (or the Order's prices, if lower),
retroactive to when the excess began. Customer will keep records reasonably sufficient to show its
compliance during the term and for **two (2) years** after it. If a signed certification is not
reasonably sufficient, Logiqum may have an independent auditor, bound by confidentiality, review those
records during normal business hours with minimal disruption and in compliance with Customer's
reasonable security and site policies (including for air-gapped sites, where Customer may provide the
evidence by offline means). Logiqum bears the cost of verification unless it reveals underpayment of
more than **five percent (5%)** for the period reviewed, in which case Customer reimburses its
reasonable cost. Verification is Logiqum's audit backstop; it is not a condition of the
license and does not require the Software to transmit data (§4–§5).

## 14. AI features

Where the Software provides AI-assisted features: **Logiqum does not use, and does not permit any model
provider to use, Customer Data or Customer inputs to train or fine-tune foundation models.** AI output may
be inaccurate or incomplete and must not be solely relied upon; Customer is responsible for validating
output before acting on it. Any third-party model providers used are disclosed in the Documentation /
Privacy Policy.

## 15. Data protection

To the extent Logiqum processes personal data on Customer's behalf, the parties' **Data Processing
Addendum** (available from Logiqum on request at contact@logiqum.com) applies and is incorporated by reference; it includes EU Standard Contractual Clauses
for any restricted transfers. Consistent with §5, the self-managed Software is designed so that Customer
log data remains within Customer's environment.

## 16. Compliance; export

Customer will comply with applicable laws in its use of the Software, including EU and US **export-control
and sanctions** laws; Customer will not use or export the Software in violation of those laws or to
embargoed destinations or restricted parties. The Software contains encryption and may be subject to
the EU Dual-Use Regulation (EU) 2021/821, the US Export Administration Regulations, and similar laws.
Customer represents that it, its Authorized Users, and its Affiliates are not named on, or owned or
controlled by a party named on, an applicable sanctions or restricted-party list, and will not use the
Software for a prohibited end use (including weapons of mass destruction or, where the law so provides,
military end use) without the authorizations the law requires.

