This Agreement is governed by the laws of **Hungary** (excluding conflict-of-laws rules and the UN
Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods). Disputes are resolved as follows:

- **Customers established in the European Union or the European Economic Area:** the parties submit to
  the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of **Budapest, Hungary**.
- **All other Customers:** any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement is finally
  settled by arbitration before the **Commercial Arbitration Court attached to the Hungarian Chamber of
  Commerce and Industry**, Budapest, under its rules in force when the proceedings start, by a sole
  arbitrator, in the **English** language, with its seat in **Budapest**.

The parties may agree in an Order to a different governing law and venue (for example, for US-based
Customers). Nothing prevents
either party from seeking injunctive or other equitable relief in any competent court for a breach or
threatened breach of the other's intellectual-property rights, of confidentiality (§11), or of §3 or
§6.1. Each party agrees that such a breach is likely to cause the other irreparable harm for which money
damages would not be an adequate remedy, and, to the extent the law of the court allows, that relief
may be sought without proving actual damage and without posting a bond.

## 18. General

Neither party may assign this Agreement without the other's consent, except to a successor of its business
(with notice). If any provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in effect. This Agreement (with any
Order, DPA, and Documentation referenced) is the entire agreement and supersedes prior understandings on
its subject. Neither party is liable for delays caused by events beyond its reasonable control. Failure to
enforce a provision is not a waiver. Notices must be in writing to the parties' designated contacts.
Customer may not assign or transfer an Entitlement except together with an assignment of this Agreement
permitted above.

**Acceptance and versions.** You accept this Agreement as follows. (a) The appliance's first-boot
screen shows this Agreement and requires an explicit acceptance; an unattended install requires an
explicit `ACCEPT_EULA=yes` in its answer file. (b) The Agent, the Converter, the Tools, and
self-deployed Software have no acceptance screen: installing or using them is acceptance, as stated
at the top of this Agreement. (c) This Agreement is always available on the product's About page and
is published with each release. A newer version applies to new installations, and to upgrades from the
time it is published with that version; if you continue to use the Software after an upgrade, you accept
the version shipped with that upgrade. Section 6.1 applies to the Converter and the Tools exactly as to
the rest of the Software, including (c) (reverse engineering) and (k) (AI-assisted replication); the
ownership of Converted Configuration stays with Customer as defined in §1.

**Agent distributions.** The Agent is also distributed with its own license text. That text and this
Agreement are intended to be consistent; where the Agent is used under a logrok Order, this Agreement
governs to the extent of any conflict, and the restrictions in §3 and §6 (including those concerning
Logiqum Interfaces between the Agent and the control plane) apply to the Agent.

**US Government end users.** The Software and Documentation are "commercial computer software" and
"commercial computer software documentation" developed exclusively at private expense. Under FAR 12.212
and DFARS 227.7202 (or equivalent agency provisions), US Government end users acquire only the rights
this Agreement grants to all other customers.

